 "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 10, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nThink about fonts.\n ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le06ob11re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn9le06ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Excuse me, are you looking for this?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: My phone! Where did you find it?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: It was on the chair where you were sitting. What did you think of the workshop, by the way? It was really beneficial, wasn't it?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah. It's designed to give you an overview of job search skills. I've learned a lot about doing a r\u00e9sum\u00e9, a cover letter and oral presentation.", "image": "engenn9le06ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Like what?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well, I learned the essentials of a r\u00e9sum\u00e9, like a concise summary of skills, strengths and accomplishments. You really need to show how you can fit into your target industry. This is made clear in the workshop.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: That's useful information, isn't it?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah. A good first impression is created by a great cover letter. It will help you stand out. Your skills and what you can bring to a company should be summarized in the cover letter. The cover letter should have four paragraphs that will cover how you got the job lead, your skills, what you can bring to the company, and how you will follow up.", "image": "engenn9le06ob11re2img06.jpg", "time": "20400", "id": 2}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: And what about presentations? Giving presentations is a necessary skill, isn't it? Employers are impressed by great presentation skills.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yes. But it's never easy to be confident when you're in front of a group, is it? I discovered that the purpose of your presentation should be made clear right from the start. Also, you should keep your presentation short. And an interesting fact that I learned about presentations is that they need to have a lot of questions so that the listeners are part of the conversation. You should engage your listeners, shouldn't you?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: All these skills are needed for a successful job search. I'm Adam, by the way.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'm Kristi. Great to meet you!", "image": "engenn9le06ob11re2img07.jpg", "time": "58000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn9le06ob11re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le06ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Job Search", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let's Review: Job Search, Job Quest", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe jobs and careers in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Simple Present Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br> You use a passive structure when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In<span class=\"strong\"> active</span> sentences, the thing doing the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing receiving the action is the object. Most sentences are active.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[Thing doing action] + [verb] + [thing receiving action]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br> Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Employers (subject)<span class=\"strong\"> advertise</span> most jobs</span> (object) <span class=\"italic\">online.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In <span class=\"strong\">passive</span> sentences, the thing receiving the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing doing the action is optionally included near the end of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the passive form if you think that the thing receiving the action is more important or should be emphasized. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use the passive form if you do not know who is doing the action or if you do not want to mention who is doing the action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[Thing receiving action] + [be] + [past participle of verb] + [by] + [thing doing action]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br> Passive sentence = (by employers) <span class=\"italic\">It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the Present Passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It's designed to give you an overview of job search skills.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This is made clear in the workshop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A good first impression is created by a great cover letter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Employers are impressed by great presentation skills.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All these skills are needed for a successful job search.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They are mainly used in speech when we want to:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not,</span> or<br><li><span class=\"strong\"> to encourage a reply </span>from the person we are speaking to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no' ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be </span>or a <span class=\"italic\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same.<br> For <span class=\"italic\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag<span class=\"italic\"> do/does or did/didn't</span>. Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Negative adverbs", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The adverbs <span class=\"italic\">never, rarely, seldom, hardly, barely and scarcely </span>have a negative sense. Even though they may be in a positive statement, the feeling of the statement is negative. We treat statements with these words like negative statements, so the question tag is normally <span class=\"strong\">positive</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" positive statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" negative statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It isn't/wasn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" is/was it??\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" modal verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It can/could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can't/couldn't it?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" negative modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It can't/couldn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can/could it?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" negative adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It never does/did\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" does/did it?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "It was really beneficial, wasn't it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's never easy to be confident when you're in front of a group, is it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should engage your listeners, shouldn't you?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "beneficial", "type": "name"}, {"content": "producing benefits ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It was really beneficial, wasn't it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "accomplishment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something done admirably or creditably", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I learned the essentials of a r\u00e9sum\u00e9, like a concise summary of skills, strengths and accomplishments.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stand out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be noticeable and different from the rest ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It will help you stand out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": 